# Quiz Arena — Notifications, Streaks & Push: Handoff Note

## What's in this feature, end to end

**Student side:**
- Notification bell next to "Welcome Back" — unread badge, wiggles while unread, opens a dropdown panel.
- Best Score stat card replaced with an animated Day Streak card (flame pulses while streak > 0).
- Real OS/phone push notifications, on top of the in-app bell.

**Admin side:**
- New "Notifications" tab — compose a broadcast, see sent history, delete one.

**Automatic notifications (no admin action needed):**
- New student signs up → personal "Welcome to Quiz Arena" ping (them only).
- New quiz added → broadcast to all students — **wiring pending**, see "Not yet done" below.

---

## File manifest — where everything goes

| File | Destination | Status |
|---|---|---|
| `notificationsService.js` | root, next to `auth.js` | new |
| `pushNotifications.js` | root, next to `auth.js` | new |
| `firebase-messaging-sw.js` | **site root**, same level as `index.html` (not inside any subfolder) | new |
| `functions/index.js` | replaces your existing `functions/index.js` | updated — your Flutterwave function is untouched, `sendNotificationPush` added below it |
| `notifications.js` | admin folder, next to `subjects.js` | new |
| `auth.js` | replaces existing | updated — fires welcome notification on signup |
| `attemptsService.js` | replaces existing | updated — added `getStreakCount()` |
| `dashboard.js` (student) | replaces existing | updated — bell, streak card, push registration |
| `dashboard.css` (student) | replaces existing | updated — bell/panel/streak styles |
| `admin.js` | replaces existing | updated — new Notifications tab wired in |
| `admin-dashboard.css` | replaces existing | updated — notification compose/list styles |

---

## Setup you still need to do (nothing here works until these are done)

1. **Firestore security rules** — add:
   - `notifications` collection: students need `read`; only admins should get `write` (your manual sends already go through the admin console, but automatic ones — welcome, new quiz — get written from client code too, so make sure your rules account for that, e.g. allow write when `request.auth.uid` matches a student creating their own welcome ping, or move those two automatic writes server-side later if you want tighter control).
   - `users/{uid}`: allow a user to `update` their own doc for `lastNotificationsSeenAt` and `fcmTokens` fields.

2. **Firestore composite indexes** — the notification queries will throw an error with a "create index" console link the first time each one runs. Click through those once (both the admin broadcast query and the student's merged broadcast+personal query need one).

3. **VAPID key** — Firebase Console → Project Settings → Cloud Messaging → Web Push certificates → generate a key pair → paste it into `VAPID_KEY` in `pushNotifications.js`. Nothing push-related works until this is real.

4. **Deploy the service worker** — `firebase-messaging-sw.js` has to sit at your site's root (same level as `index.html`), not in a subfolder — a service worker can only control pages within its own scope.

5. **Deploy the Cloud Function** — no new dependencies needed, your existing `functions/package.json` already covers everything (`firebase-admin` gives `admin.messaging()`, `firebase-functions` already includes the `/v2/firestore` trigger). Just:
   ```
   firebase deploy --only functions
   ```
   Without this deployed, tokens get saved to Firestore but nothing ever actually sends — the Cloud Function is the only piece that talks to FCM. `sendNotificationPush` is now in the same `index.js` as your `verifyFlutterwavePurchase` function, untouched.

---

## Bugs found and fixed during this build

1. **Bell panel invisible / stuck "inside the purple box"** — `.dashboard-hero` has `overflow: hidden` (needed to clip the decorative parallax shapes at its rounded corners), which was also silently clipping the dropdown panel nested inside it. Fixed by having the panel append directly to `document.body` with `position: fixed`, positioned via JS from the bell's actual screen coordinates — same escape-the-clipped-parent trick your `dangerDialog.js` already uses for its overlay.

2. **New students saw old broadcast history** — `getRecentNotificationsForUser` had no lower bound, so a brand-new signup would see every broadcast ever sent. Fixed by filtering broadcasts to `createdAt > student's account createdAt`. Existing students are unaffected since their account predates all current broadcasts.

3. **Duplicate outside-click / scroll listeners** — a student bouncing back to the dashboard multiple times in one session (`renderStudentDashboard()` called again) would otherwise stack up multiple `document`/`window` listeners over time. Fixed with module-level handler references that get removed before a new one is bound.

4. **Empty-token-array crash risk** — sending a push to zero tokens (e.g., a broadcast before anyone has granted permission yet) is guarded against in the Cloud Function before calling `sendEachForMulticast`.

## Known limitations (not bugs, just things worth knowing)

- **No live updates while the tab is open** — the in-app bell list is a one-time fetch per dashboard load, not a real-time listener, consistent with how the rest of this app already works (no `onSnapshot` anywhere else either). A student with the dashboard open when a new broadcast goes out won't see it in the bell until they reload — though they *will* still get the actual phone/OS push regardless, since that's a separate delivery path.
- **iOS Safari** only supports web push for sites added to the home screen (iOS 16.4+) — a student browsing in regular mobile Safari won't be able to grant permission at all. Nothing to fix, just a platform limit worth setting expectations around.
- **Repeated `markNotificationsSeen` writes** — every bell open writes a fresh timestamp, even if nothing changed since last time. Harmless, just a minor inefficiency if it ever matters at scale.

## Not yet done

- **"New quiz added" broadcast isn't wired in yet.** `sendNewQuizNotification(quizTitle)` exists and is ready in `notificationsService.js`, but nothing calls it — I need `quizzes.js` to hook it in after a successful quiz save, matching your actual field names (`title` vs `name`) and the exact spot the `addDoc` call succeeds.